{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 139,
    "dDurationMs": 4251,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We see particle-like behavior every day: drop\na ball on the ground and it follows a single"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4390,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "trajectory, leave your giraffe parked on the\nstreet and when you come back, it's still"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8150,
    "dDurationMs": 1450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there, just one giraffe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9600,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And we see wave behavior, too!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11800,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Toot your horn, and waves spread out through\nthe air, carrying sound to the ears of anyone"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15800,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "around."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16800,
    "dDurationMs": 3959,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or drive a boat through water, and waves travel\noutwards along the surface."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20759,
    "dDurationMs": 2150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But when it comes to the physics of the very\nsmall,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22909,
    "dDurationMs": 3141,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what we see is a wave-particle duality."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26050,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sometimes very small things (we're talking\nelectrons \u0026 protons here) behave like particles,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30670,
    "dDurationMs": 1659,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and sometimes they behave like waves!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32329,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Flip-floppers!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33329,
    "dDurationMs": 5131,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, if you release an electron, it'll\ntravel outward as a wave through the room,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38460,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but when it hits the wall, it'll only hit\nin one place - you started with one electron,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42510,
    "dDurationMs": 1170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "after all!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43680,
    "dDurationMs": 2690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what if sound had a wave-particle duality?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46370,
    "dDurationMs": 4419,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you shouted, the sound waves would spread\noutwards in all directions, but only one person"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50789,
    "dDurationMs": 1521,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "could hear what you said!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52310,
    "dDurationMs": 3810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or when you drove your boat through the water,\nthe waves would travel like normal, but only"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56120,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hit the shore in one place!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58010,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now that would make for some pretty boring\nsurfing!"
    } ]
  } ]
}
